2026-10-09T01:05:32.2143268Z   ok   the inferred estimator reads a real defrost as a PERFECT interval
2026-10-09T01:05:32.2143377Z   ok   an over-1 ratio can no longer park the derate above 1.0
2026-10-09T01:05:32.2143476Z   ok   five defrosting minutes in thirty is a duty of 1/6
2026-10-09T01:05:32.2143552Z   ok   and the interval counts as observed
2026-10-09T01:05:32.2143708Z   ok   a quiet interval is duty zero AND observed — that is real evidence
2026-10-09T01:05:32.2143812Z   ok   an unreadable flag yields duty zero but NOT observed
2026-10-09T01:05:32.2143926Z   ok   a defrost spanning an interval boundary keeps its second half
2026-10-09T01:05:32.2144056Z   ok   a sample stamped before the last does not subtract from the on-time
2026-10-09T01:05:32.2144135Z   ok   zero duty is no derate at all
2026-10-09T01:05:32.2144224Z   ok   the derate is 1 - duty x the loss multiplier
2026-10-09T01:05:32.2144338Z   ok   more duty is always a deeper derate, never a shallower one
2026-10-09T01:05:32.2144458Z   ok   and it is bounded below, so a latched flag cannot zero the pump
2026-10-09T01:05:32.2144554Z   ok   a measured bucket derates from its counted duty
2026-10-09T01:05:32.2144688Z   ok   and a measurement is never averaged with an inference of the same thing
